INT. PARKING GARAGE - LEVEL 3 - NIGHT

Concrete columns. Flickering fluorescents. A single sedan idles.

BRENDAN MWANGI, 40s, sits in the sedan, engine running. He checks his watch. His partner, SOLEDAD ARRIAGA, 30s, leans on a column nearby, smoking. She flicks ash and watches the ramp.

BRENDAN
(through the window)
He's late.

SOLEDAD
He'll come.

BRENDAN
You said that an hour ago.

She shrugs and drops the cigarette. A set of headlights sweeps the ramp. She straightens. He kills the engine. A black van rolls in and stops. The side door slides open.

TOBIAS KESSLER-ADEYEMI, 50s, steps out in a long coat, flanked by a stocky man in sunglasses. He walks over slowly. Brendan climbs out of the sedan.

TOBIAS
Gentlemen. Lady.

SOLEDAD
You're an hour late.

TOBIAS
Traffic.

BRENDAN
Do you have it?

Tobias smiles. He reaches into his coat. Brendan tenses. Soledad's hand moves to her hip.

TOBIAS
Relax.

He pulls out an envelope. Holds it up. She takes a step. The stocky man steps with her. Tobias lowers the envelope.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
First, the money.

Brendan opens the trunk. A duffel. He unzips it, shows the bundles. Tobias nods.

SOLEDAD
Now the envelope.

Tobias hands it over. She tears it open. Photographs. Her face goes cold.

SOLEDAD (CONT'D)
These are of my daughter.

TOBIAS
Yes.

She draws her gun. The stocky man draws his. Brendan freezes. Tobias raises both hands, still smiling.

TOBIAS (CONT'D)
Now we all understand each other.
